{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1611","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1611","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1611\",\"parent_revision\":\"32411d6feb0f3372c72a6e0b71d4ff28997b475f586ddff0cd0745333c1d0456\",\"root_revision\":\"32411d6feb0f3372c72a6e0b71d4ff28997b475f586ddff0cd0745333c1d0456\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`append_task_section(plan_id, task_id, section_name, content)` stores content in different fields depending on which backend is active:\\n\\n- `LocalYamlTaskProvider` (`local_yaml.py:490\u2013527`): accumulates content in `context_notes` using `## {section_name}` heading\\n- `InMemoryTaskProvider` (`memory.py:465\u2013490`): same \u2014 `context_notes`\\n- `GitHubTaskProvider` (`github_task.py:444\u2013451`): appends to `body` field directly\\n\\nAn agent calling `append_task_section(plan_id, task_id, \\\"Findings\\\", content)` with the local backend gets content in `context_notes[\\\"## Findings\\\"]`. The same call with the GitHub backend puts content in `body`. The Protocol docstring (now updated) documents this divergence but does not resolve it.\\n\\nEvidence: Impact analysis for #1491 confirmed via source code read (2026-04-06). PR branch: `fix/test-isolation-and-hook-format`, commit `efdb702`.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] All three backends produce content retrievable via `read_task` at the same key path for any `section_name` value\\n- [ ] Conformance test `test_append_task_section` exercises `section_name=\\\"Work Log\\\"` (arbitrary, non-field name) and asserts storage outcome\\n- [ ] Protocol docstring updated to reflect the canonical storage contract once decided\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using the SAM task backend**, I want to **append_task_section to store content in the same field regardless of backend** so that **agent code behaves consistently whether the local, memory, or GitHub backend is active**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Impact analysis for #1491, session 2026-04-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-06\\n- **Related**: #1491\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### RT-ICA Snapshot (2026-04-07)\\n\\n**Goal:** Define and enforce a single storage target for `append_task_section()` content across all task provider backends.\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|-----------|--------|----------|\\n| Divergence exists in current code | MISSING | `local_yaml.py`, `memory.py`, `github_task.py` do not exist in main branch \u2014 these are from PR #1613 branch only |\\n| PR #1613 status | AVAILABLE | PR #1613 open, adds `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` Protocol; implementations NOT included in PR |\\n| Protocol file exists | AVAILABLE | `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` added by PR #1613 |\\n| Decision (Option A/B/C) | MISSING \u2014 design decision required | Human input needed |\\n\\n**Decision: BLOCKED \u2014 two reasons:**\\n1. Implementation files (`local_yaml.py` etc.) don't exist in main \u2014 this is a design decision for code not yet written\\n2. Option A/B/C choice requires human direction\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Missing-guardrail \u2014 pre-implementation design contract\\n\\nThis is NOT a defect in existing code. The backends are not yet implemented in main. This issue should drive the Protocol contract before the backends are written.\\n\\n**5-Whys:**\\n1. Why do backends store sections differently? \u2192 No contract was specified when the Protocol was designed\\n2. Why no contract? \u2192 Protocol was designed abstractly without all three implementations present\\n3. Why does this matter now? \u2192 PR #1613 adds the Protocol; implementations should follow a consistent contract\\n4. Why is this tracked separately? \u2192 PR #1613 explicitly punted this decision to #1611\\n5. **Root fix**: Define the canonical storage target IN the Protocol before implementing the three providers\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Role | Notes |\\n|------|------|-------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` (PR #1613) | Protocol | Needs canonical storage field documented |\\n| Future `local_yaml.py` | Provider implementation | Should implement to the contract |\\n| Future `memory.py` | Provider implementation | Should implement to the contract |\\n| Future `github_task.py` | Provider implementation | Should implement to the contract |\\n| Tests (any file testing `append_task_section`) | Test | Conformance test should be added here |\\n\\n### Option Trade-off Analysis\\n\\n| Option | Effort | Risk | Recommended if... |\\n|--------|--------|------|------------------|\\n| A \u2014 Canonicalize to `context_notes` | Medium | Low | API stability is priority; `context_notes` is semantic metadata |\\n| B \u2014 Canonicalize to `body` | Medium | Medium | User-facing visibility is priority; content should appear in issue body |\\n| C \u2014 Conformance test only | Small | Low | Deferring; minimizes pre-implementation contract |\\n\\n**Option A recommendation basis:** 2-of-3 planned implementations already use `context_notes`. Defining `context_notes` as canonical in the Protocol before any implementation is written is lower risk than retrofitting later.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` (via PR #1613 branch)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Small (S)** \u2014 Protocol docstring update + conformance test. Actual implementation effort is in the future PR implementing the three backends.\\n\\n### Open Question (BLOCKS planning)\\n\\n**Which option?** Human decision required. Recommendation: Option A (`context_notes`) since it aligns with the 2-of-3 planned pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Decision Required\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nChoose one canonical storage target:\\n\\n**Option A \u2014 Canonicalize to `context_notes`**: Fix `GitHubTaskProvider` to accumulate in its equivalent of `context_notes`. Requires verifying what field name the GitHub backend exposes via `read_task`.\\n\\n**Option B \u2014 Canonicalize to `body`**: Fix `LocalYamlTaskProvider` and `InMemoryTaskProvider` to write to `body`. Simpler for GitHub backend but requires changing the YAML read-modify-write target.\\n\\n**Option C \u2014 Leave divergence, add conformance test**: Accept per-backend behavior, add a conformance test that asserts `read_task` always returns the content regardless of backend, without asserting which field.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5866fa189f52c4a43c1bd180f193a7e59038a2196103d2fa3a51b994ff481965\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrqGA\"}"}